### ─── CATEGORIES ─────────────────────────────────────────────

### 1. Create category — Electronics
POST http://localhost:3004/v1/categories
Authorization: Bearer mock-token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Electronics",
  "description": "Phones, laptops, tablets and accessories"
}

###

### 2. Create category — Clothing
POST http://localhost:3004/v1/categories
Authorization: Bearer mock-token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Clothing",
  "description": "T-shirts, jackets, shoes and more"
}

###

### 3. List all categories
GET http://localhost:3004/v1/categories
Authorization: Bearer mock-token

###

### 4. Get category by ID  (replace with real UUID from step 1)
GET http://localhost:3004/v1/categories/ad7ef565-00c0-4490-96df-ec44871b7d72
Authorization: Bearer mock-token


### ─── PRODUCTS ────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 5. Create product — iPhone 15 Pro (replace categoryId with UUID from step 1)
POST http://localhost:3004/v1/products
Authorization: Bearer mock-token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "iPhone 15 Pro",
  "description": "Apple flagship smartphone with titanium frame and A17 Pro chip",
  "price": 999.99,
  "stock": 50,
  "image": "https://store.storeimages.cdn-apple.com/iphone15pro.jpg",
  "specs": {
    "brand": "Apple",
    "model": "iPhone 15 Pro",
    "chip": "A17 Pro",
    "color": "Natural Titanium",
    "weight": "187g"
  },
  "categoryId": "ad7ef565-00c0-4490-96df-ec44871b7d72"
}

###

### 6. Create product — Samsung Galaxy S24 (replace categoryId)
POST http://localhost:3004/v1/products
Authorization: Bearer mock-token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Samsung Galaxy S24",
  "description": "Samsung flagship with Snapdragon 8 Gen 3 and 50MP camera",
  "price": 799.99,
  "stock": 30,
  "image": "https://image.samsung.com/is/image/samsung/galaxy-s24.jpg",
  "specs": {
    "brand": "Samsung",
    "model": "Galaxy S24",
    "processor": "Snapdragon 8 Gen 3",
    "color": "Onyx Black",
    "weight": "167g"
  },
  "categoryId": "ad7ef565-00c0-4490-96df-ec44871b7d72"
}

###

### 7. Create product — minimal (no image/specs/category — uses defaults)
POST http://localhost:3004/v1/products
Authorization: Bearer mock-token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Basic T-Shirt",
  "description": "100% cotton unisex t-shirt available in multiple sizes",
  "price": 19.99,
  "stock": 200
}

###

### 8. List products (page 1, default limit 10)
GET http://localhost:3004/v1/products?page=1&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer mock-token

###

### 9. Filter products by category  (replace with real UUID)
GET http://localhost:3004/v1/products?categoryId=ad7ef565-00c0-4490-96df-ec44871b7d72
Authorization: Bearer mock-token

###

### 10. Get product by ID  (replace with real UUID from step 5)
GET http://localhost:3004/v1/products/4b21efbb-481d-4f7b-9497-7eb7ade12255
Authorization: Bearer mock-token

###

### 11. Update product  (replace with real UUID)
PUT http://localhost:3004/v1/products/4b21efbb-481d-4f7b-9497-7eb7ade12255
Authorization: Bearer mock-token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "price": 899.99,
  "stock": 45,
  "specs": {
    "brand": "Apple",
    "model": "iPhone 15 Pro",
    "chip": "A17 Pro",
    "color": "Desert Titanium",
    "weight": "187g"
  }
}

###

### 12. Validation error — invalid specs key
POST http://localhost:3004/v1/products
Authorization: Bearer mock-token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bad Product",
  "description": "This should fail because specs has a disallowed key",
  "price": 9.99,
  "specs": {
    "invalidKey": "oops"
  }
}

###

### 13. Validation error — invalid image URL
POST http://localhost:3004/v1/products
Authorization: Bearer mock-token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bad Image",
  "description": "This should fail because image is not a valid URL",
  "price": 9.99,
  "image": "not-a-url"
}

###

### 14. Delete product  (replace with real UUID)
DELETE http://localhost:3004/v1/products/4b21efbb-481d-4f7b-9497-7eb7ade12255
Authorization: Bearer mock-token
